  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The maximum probability for Lottery A is 100% (since it offers 2400 Euros with certainty). For Lottery B, the maximum single probability is 66% (for winning 2400 Euros). The remaining outcomes have probabilities of 33% and 1%, so 66% is the highest probability in Lottery B. Therefore, the maximum probability is higher for Lottery A (100%) than for Lottery B (66%). According to the decision reason, Lottery A should be preferred because it has the higher maximum probability.",
